.TH MX-SYSTEM-SOUNDS 1 "2026-08-30" "MX Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mx-system-sounds \- configure system sound events for the Xfce desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mx-system-sounds
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mx-system-sounds
is a graphical utility for MX Linux that lets a user enable or disable
Xfce event sounds, choose a sound theme, and customize individual sound
events from a single dialog.
.PP
The dialog covers three areas:
.TP
.B Xfce Event Sounds
Mirrors the "Event Sounds" settings found in Appearance Settings; either
tool may be used interchangeably.
.TP
.B Session Sounds
MX-specific login and logout sound settings, enabled independently of
the main Xfce event sounds.
.TP
.B Custom Sounds
Selection of the sound theme, and of custom login/logout sounds. The
currently selected sound can be previewed, and a theme's default sound
(if any) can be restored.
.SH OPTIONS
This application has no documented command-line options. The graphical
interface provides all operations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/MX-Linux/mx-system-sounds/mx-login-logout_sounds.conf
Per-user login/logout sound preferences.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/mx-system-sounds
Installed HTML help, images, and license documentation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR startupsound-mx (1)
